 States]]\n__NOTOC__\n==Ingredients==\n*2 cans (2 [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]] + 8 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]] / 900 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) [[Cookbook:Yam|yams]] or sweet potatoes, drained (or 4 lb / 1.8 kg cooked, peeled, and sliced yams)\n*⅔ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Orange|orange]] juice\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] grated orange rind\n*½ cup [[Cookbook:Bourbon|bourbon]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoons]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*1 teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n*4 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]], melted\n*⅓ cup packed brown [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*3 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]] yolks\n*Fresh [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]] to taste\n\n===Topping===\n*⅔ cup packed [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n*¼ lb butter, melted\n*1 cup (about 4 oz / 110 g) [[Cookbook:Pecan|pecans]], chopped \n*1 teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# In mixing bowl with electric [[Cookbook:Mixer|mixer]], beat yams. Add in remaining main ingredients, beating until mixture is light and fluffy. Butter a 12-inch porcelain quiche dish or a shallow 2 quart [[Cookbook:Baking Dish|casserole dish]] (7x11 inches / 18 x 28 cm). Pour in yam mixture, smoothing top evenly.\n# Make praline topping by mixing all ingredients together in small bowl. Spread evenly over the yams. May be refrigerated covered overnight.\n# [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] at 350°F (180°C) for 45–50 minutes or until golden brown and bubbly.\n# Remove from oven and let stand 10 minutes before serving.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for casserole]]\n[[Category:Thanksgiving recipes]]\n[[Category:United States recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using yam]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pecan]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Baked recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg yolk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bourbon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using orange 